# e8-mare-claim — the ride log for tasks/e8-mare-claim-physics.md
# Produced by artifacts/e8-mare-claim-physics/ride.mjs (public door surface only: standing orders
# in, the rider view out). Node v23.11.1, darwin, contract e8-mare-claim, bench seed e8-mare-claim-01.
#
# WHAT TO LOOK FOR
#   · GRAVITY-SCALED LOBS — `blast_at` events carry lob={reach:24,airTime:1.68}. Off gravity that
#     reach is Balance.blast.range = 10m and the hang 0.7s; this contract's 2.4x arc is what makes
#     a 20m BLAST_AT legal at all (at 1.0x the same order is refused OUT_OF_RANGE).
#   · AIR DRAIN — now.air.suit.seconds falls one second per second outside a breathing dome and
#     refills at 4/s inside one; drainedTotal / emptySeconds / breathlessPans are cumulative.
#   · THE DOMES — each pad's air dial falls while an outlaw stands on it (breached:true) and seals
#     when the pad clears; `breaches` counts the sieges.
#   · THE REGOLITH RUN — `regolith_ground_worked` fires the first time each authored ground is
#     panned ON SUIT AIR. A breathless pan is counted in breathlessPans and credited to nothing.
#   · THE SECURE — the claim cannot be offered a secure until regolith.complete is true.
#
# THREE RIDES, ONE SEED:
#   1. IDLE       — the null floor: no orders at all. Suit empties, no ground is ever worked.
#   2. FLOOR      — the scripted rider from its own starting kit, no buffs. Works 2 grounds on
#                   air and opens the latch at t=5.3s, then dies at wave 2 (this map's null floor,
#                   assets/contracts/null-floors.json), so it never reaches the wave-20 boundary.
#                   No rider has ever secured this contract: winnability-receipts.json says
#                   {"contractId":"e8-mare-claim","status":"unclaimed"}.
#   3. HARNESS    — the same policy with an immortal hero (twin-banks-hash-probe idiom), so the
#                   ride outlives the null floor and reaches the secure boundary. SECURED at wave
#                   20 with the latch open. NOT a floor result and never to be read as one.
#
# A/B ON THE LATCH, same seed and same policy, measured 2026-09-04:
#   latch CLOSED (the gate asking six grounds, five worked) -> no secure offered at wave 20; the
#     ride ran on to wave 27 and died. secured:false eventLogHash fnv1a32:7f2c4650
#   latch OPEN   (the gate asking one, five worked)         -> offered at wave 20, banked.
#     secured:true  waves:20 eventLogHash fnv1a32:fea8b6d1


